This project routes LLM traffic through **Headroom** (`agent-90` profile, ~90% token savings, persistent memory).

## Status checks

```bash
headroom doctor
headroom install status
scripts/verify-memory-setup.sh
```

## Cursor setup (required once)

Proxy must be healthy (`headroom install status`). Then in **Cursor → Settings → Models**:

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Override OpenAI Base URL | `http://127.0.0.1:8787/p/gandom_galery_shop/v1` |
| Anthropic base URL (if shown) | `http://127.0.0.1:8787/p/gandom_galery_shop` |

Use your normal provider API keys — Headroom forwards and compresses.

Re-print project URLs anytime:

```bash
headroom wrap cursor --no-proxy
```

## Other agents (already configured globally)

- **Codex** — routed via `~/.codex/config.toml` (`headroom init -g codex`)
- **Claude Code** — routed via `~/.claude/settings.json` (when Claude CLI installed)

## With graphify

1. `graphify query "<question>"` first (scoped subgraph, low tokens)
2. Read only lines you will edit
3. `graphify update .` after code changes
4. `headroom dashboard` — view compression savings
